# Paper Design Components

## Design Tokens

All visual values (colors, radii, typography, spacing, shadows) are defined in
`design/tokens.md`. **Always read tokens.md** before creating new designs or
components. Never invent values — use the token file as the source of truth.

## Component Library

Reusable HTML templates for Paper MCP live in `design/components/`. These are
the single source of truth for shared UI elements across all Paper pages and
artboards.

### App Components

| Component | File | Placeholders |
|-----------|------|-------------|
| Header | `header.html` | None (adjust active nav color after insert) |
| Page Header | `page-header.html` | `{{TITLE}}`, `{{SUBTITLE}}`, `{{TAB_1..3}}` |
| Avatar Popup | `avatar-popup.html` | `{{INITIALS}}`, `{{FULL_NAME}}`, `{{EMAIL}}` |
| Bento Card | `bento-card.html` | `{{CARD_NAME}}` (empty shell) |
| Danger Zone | `danger-zone-card.html` | `{{TITLE}}`, `{{DESCRIPTION}}`, `{{BUTTON_TEXT}}` |
| Input Field | `input-field.html` | `{{LABEL}}`, `{{VALUE}}` |
| Button | `button.html` | `{{LABEL}}` (4 variants: Primary, Outline, Danger, Auth Submit) |

### Auth Components

| Component | File | Placeholders |
|-----------|------|-------------|
| Auth Layout | `auth-layout.html` | None (structural shell, insert children) |
| Logo | `logo.html` | None (static) |
| Google Button | `google-button.html` | None (static) |
| Divider | `divider.html` | `{{TEXT}}` |
| Testimonial | `testimonial-panel.html` | `{{ICON_SVG}}`, `{{QUOTE}}`, `{{AUTHOR}}`, `{{ROLE}}` |
| Auth Footer | `auth-footer-link.html` | `{{TEXT}}`, `{{LINK_TEXT}}` |

All files are in `design/components/`.

## Rules

1. **Read tokens first.** Before any design work, read `design/tokens.md` for
   correct values. Do not use hardcoded values that differ from the tokens.

2. **Always read the template** before inserting a shared element. Use the Read
   tool to get the HTML from `design/components/<name>.html`, then pass it to
   Paper's `write_html`.

3. **Never hand-write shared elements.** If a component template exists, use it.
   Do not recreate the HTML from memory or screenshots.

4. **Replace placeholders** before passing to `write_html`. Read the HTML file,
   do string replacements for `{{PLACEHOLDER}}` values, then insert.

5. **Active nav highlighting.** The Header template defaults to "Dashboard" as
   active (color `#09090B`). When inserting on a different page, update the
   active nav item after insertion:
   - Active item: `color: #09090B`
   - Inactive items: `color: #71717A`
   Use `set_text_content` or `update_styles` to adjust after inserting.

6. **Button variants.** The `button.html` file contains four variants in HTML
   comments. Copy only the variant you need, not the entire file.

7. **Adding new components.** When a new reusable element is identified:
   - Extract it from Paper via `get_jsx` (inline-styles format)
   - Convert JSX to plain HTML (camelCase -> kebab-case, remove `boxSizing`)
   - Save to `design/components/<name>.html`
   - Update the table above

8. **Updating a component.** When a component's design changes:
   - Update the HTML file in `design/components/`
   - On the current Paper page, find all instances by `layer-name` using
     `get_tree_summary` and replace them via `write_html` mode `replace`
